      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cambuci only became an official neighborhood in 1906 after a wave of industrialization drew Italian and Syrian‑Lebanese workers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://saopaulosecreto.com/en/what-to-do-in-cambuci-sp/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the 1924 Revolution, the São Joaquim Parish served as a strategic trench for rebels, surviving bomb damage that knocked down one tower.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://saopaulosecreto.com/en/what-to-do-in-cambuci-sp/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Mesquita Brasil, opened in 1929, is the first mosque in Latin America and welcomes visitors to admire its distinctive architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
